whitened: mean e^T C^-1 e per degree of freedom; about 1 when the covariance matches the actual error. unflagged excludes pairs whose pure-IMU prior is off by more than 50 mm.
prior_whitened checks the prior P alone against groundtruth. nis is the first-iteration r^T (P + R)^-1 r without groundtruth; it tests P + R together (mean per dof and median over the chi-square median both about 1 when consistent) and is also raised by bias, wrong correspondences and linearization. Unobserved directions are dropped from nis and its degrees of freedom.
